+// A page turned into a heading of another page (/api/filetree/doc2Heading) reads as that heading. Doc2Heading keeps
+// the page's id for the heading, moves it into the target page, drops its title, type and tags, and writes the target
+// page; the source page's file it removes raw (box.Remove) and drops from no cache. The block attribute entry a read
+// cached for the page block names the source page as the page it copies, and the read check asks only whether that
+// page was raised since. Nothing raises it: its file was removed outside WriteTree, and the write that now holds the
+// block, the target page's, raises the target page. So getBlockAttrs, finding the block's entry under the same
+// notebook's key, serves the page's attributes from before the conversion (title, type doc) while the file holds the
+// heading without them, and keeps serving them until something stores the block again.
+//
+// Fault at df08f4e: kernel/cache/ial.go GetBlockIALInBox checks only entry.rootID's version, never whether the block
+// still lives in that page; kernel/model/heading.go Doc2Heading :317 removes the page's file without a raise.
+func TestDocToHeadingServesTheHeadingsAttributes(t *testing.T) {
+	f := setupMoveCacheTest(t)
+	const srcID, targetID, pivotID = "20261017150001-docsrce", "20261017150002-doctrgt", "20261017150021-pivotpa"
